---
description: Keep rollout reports and decision reviews tied to evidence, with limits stated.
globs: "**/*decision*,**/*rollout*,**/*review*"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Claims need evidence

When you write a rollout report or review:

- Every claim has a source, a date and a population.
- Unknown values are written as unknown. Never fill a gap with a plausible number.
- Usage and outcomes go in separate sections.
- Pair every speed measure with a quality measure.
- List what cannot be attributed to the tool.
- A recommendation names its owner and the date it will be reviewed.
- Thresholds are set before the period. Do not move one after seeing the data without logging why.
